in 2011 and converted to SVG fonts in 2019 by Windell H. Oskay,
www.evilmadscientist.com. Contents adapted from
emergent.unpythonic.net/software/hershey by way of "Hershey Fonts in SVG"
by Marty McGuire (http://www.thingiverse.com/thing:6168).

The Hershey Fonts are a set of vector fonts with a liberal license.

